@*
    A whole condition, as the list a reader meets under a heading.

    The outermost "All of" is not drawn. A heading already says what the list is - "Offered to", and
    then everything under it - so a first line saying "ALL OF" over that is the page telling you the
    default twice, on almost every civic in the game, before anything it actually says.

    Only the outermost, and only when it is an "all". A nested group is a real narrowing of the one
    above it and has to say which kind it is; and an "Any of" at the top is not the default, so
    dropping its word would turn a list of alternatives into a list of requirements.
*@

<ul class="sem-conditions">
    @foreach (var part in Top)
    {
        <ConditionBullets Node="@part" />
    }
</ul>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    public required DesignSession Session { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The condition to draw.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public required ConditionOutline Node { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The bullets to draw at the top, which is the condition itself unless it is an "all".</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<ConditionOutline> Top =>
        Node.Join is ConditionJoin.All ? Node.Parts : [Node];
}
